node_modules/
.DS_Store
dist/
build/
.env
*.log
# Runtime state written by the guard and its host hook — never committed
server/keep-alive.lock
server/keep-alive.out


# Evidence packs are staged with `git add -f` (see the pack READMEs; a pack that carries a pack-check.py
# fails when one of its own files is untracked - it is a PER-PACK tool, not one of the scripts/ tools, so
# it protects only the packs that carry it). Until 2026-10-22 a negation here un-ignored every evidence log so a
# pack's own log could not be dropped silently - but that is exactly what let `git add -A` sweep
# ANOTHER member's live log into an unrelated commit (measured 2026-10-21; it cost a force-push).
# gitignore cannot tell a filed pack log from one still being written, so evidence logs are ignored
# like every other log and force-added deliberately. The original defect (a pack that CITES a log it
# never committed) is caught by a pack's own pack-check.py where the pack has one, and always by reading
# the staged list both ways - which is the only check that covers every pack.

# The login-hook check writes its one-line status BESIDE the log it appends to, and the log is
# ignored by `*.log` while the status file was not: it rode a branch into a PR diff (measured
# 2026-10-29). A runtime artifact of a host hook is not a repository file.
*.log.status
